Here's the RDF output based on the described image scenes:

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Foggy scene with vehicle and child" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian .
:actor2 a :Vehicle .

:weather1 a :FoggyCondition .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Soccer ball in the middle of the road" .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of collision with child crossing" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Vehicle distracted by visibility issues" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.70"^^xsd:float .
```

